Sval: a write to a native host that stopped reading ends the port quietly

NativeApp._startWrite reports every write failure with Cu.reportError. A
host that has closed its stdin, or exited, makes the write fail with "File
closed" (Subprocess.ERROR_END_OF_FILE), the same end of file _startRead and
_cleanup already treat as an ordinary disconnect. Extensions that message
their host on tab changes, such as iCloud Passwords, logged it as an error.
NativeApp is Mozilla's, so no chrome API reaches it.

diff --git a/toolkit/components/extensions/NativeMessaging.sys.mjs b/toolkit/components/extensions/NativeMessaging.sys.mjs
index 0b7c2f33a8..e953b579cc 100644
--- a/toolkit/components/extensions/NativeMessaging.sys.mjs
+++ b/toolkit/components/extensions/NativeMessaging.sys.mjs
@@ -292,7 +292,11 @@ export class NativeApp extends EventEmitter {
         this._startWrite();
       })
       .catch(err => {
-        Cu.reportError(err.message);
+        // A host that has closed its end ends the port the way end of file
+        // on its stdout does in _startRead: quietly.
+        if (err.errorCode != lazy.Subprocess.ERROR_END_OF_FILE) {
+          Cu.reportError(err.message);
+        }
         this._cleanup(err);
       });
   }
